A useful trick: the % operator gives you the remainder after dividing.

4 % 2 = 0  (divides evenly — even)
5 % 2 = 1  (has a remainder — odd)

for i in range(6):
    if i % 2 == 0:
        print(i, "is even")
    else:
        print(i, "is odd")

This checks every number from 0 to 5.

